{
  "_comment": [
    "A world held at the cold end, and the clearest case of a word meaning its own part of whatever it is",
    "laid on (world model 3). Temperature is what makes an Age frozen at all and is the core; everything",
    "else is what *this* frozen Age happens to be like, drawn from the pool.",
    "",
    "It declares no aspects, so it reaches whatever its claims reach -- the climate, the air, the sky. That",
    "is the whole of what attachment then does: `frozen climate` lands the temperature and nothing else,",
    "`frozen sky` a pale vault and a small distant sun, and `a frozen Age` puts every one of them in play.",
    "One word rather than four, and no rule anywhere had to say so.",
    "",
    "`colour` is one name across every aspect that has one, so the pale draw reaches the vault, the air and",
    "the clouds together. The small draw is the sun's and the moon's alone, a quarter to a third of vanilla's,",
    "which is a far one: a bare `size` reached everything with a size, and a frozen Age came out with",
    "minuscule land and minuscule creatures.",
    "",
    "The ground may be frozen too, drawn by tag from whatever a world can be made of that is -- snow and ice,",
    "never the packed or blue ice a broad word is fenced from. The rock is only offered, since a world built",
    "of ice is a stronger thing to have said than a world dressed in snow. The sea and biomes lean cold.",
    "",
    "**`icy` folded in** (the readings spike, 2026-09-29): its aurora, its refusal of a molten sea, its lean to",
    "ice spikes and its offers across the rainbow, the air, the vault and the aurora are frozen's now. Two words",
    "that looked as though they should differ and did not, which is the case for having one."
  ],
